+The follow-up Bridge dependency refresh addresses the 33 reported alerts. Full npm audit reports zero vulnerabilities; see the bridge repository's `docs/dependency-security.md` for resolved versions and validation.
+
+## Image descriptions and matrix updates
+
+A persisted scan triggers the parent matrix refresh after scan, apply, or restore. A task receives scan evidence only when a task was selected. Successful page writes and failed scan/evidence persistence remain separate outcomes.
+
+`preview` with `reviewImages: true` creates an unchanged, expiring preview for all uniquely identified source images. `describe-image` takes `imageSource` and `previewToken`, resolves the authorized page, and generates a suggestion from the actual image. It does not modify the source or the cached preview. The instructor edits the suggested short alt and long description, updates the preview, reviews it, and explicitly applies it.
+
+`revise-preview` accepts `altEdits` entries with `src`, `text`, and optional `longDescription`. Long descriptions are escaped plain text, limited to 12,000 characters, displayed beside the image and associated with `aria-describedby`. Existing associations and unrelated page bytes are preserved. Updating or removing a description affects only the generated block. Pending edits disable Apply until incorporated into the reviewed preview.
+
+## Expanded validation
+
+The complete Conductor client and server builds passed locally and in the Linux Docker build. Browser validation on the normal source-built application confirmed authenticated startup, page actions, automatic matrix refresh, correct no-task wording, actual-image description generation, reviewed editing, apply/rescan, and persistence of the long description after a fresh CXone read.
+
+Live advanced-agent tests exercised both Ollama primary and OpenAI fallback. Each corrected duplicate IDs and skipped heading levels, reducing the fixture from two findings to zero. The heading tool accepts exactly one existing heading and levels 1–6, preserving attributes and content. Additional cases covered tables, links, and already-correct content. Strategy-only Local Lab output can retain findings; it is not equivalent to the full deterministic-plus-agent pipeline.
+
+Axe incomplete checks retain informational severity and map to manual review, even when the rule's potential impact is critical. They are not reported as confirmed accessibility failures.
+
+Transparent source images are composited onto white for inference so black chemical labels remain visible. The source image is never changed. Table-header inference requires an explicitly marked header row; ordinary first-row data is left for reviewer-supplied headers. Table associations support grouped columns and row spans and allocate IDs across the whole page.
